@host = http://localhost:5174

### Check PostgreSQL connection
GET {{host}}/api/database/status
Accept: application/json

### Get modules from PostgreSQL
GET {{host}}/api/modules
Accept: application/json

### Get users from PostgresSQL
Get {{host}}/api/users
Accept: application/json


### Get users from PostgresSQL
GET {{host}}/api/certificates/21f26bda-2f2d-43f5-bf80-3b1bc5dd12fd
Accept: application/json

### Get all certificates
GET {{host}}/api/exercises
Accept: application/json

### ---- Admin: Students (needs an Admin / SuperAdmin / Reviewer token) ----
@adminToken = paste-a-jwt-here

### List students (filters: search, moduleId, status, page, pageSize)
GET {{host}}/api/admin/students?status=Needs support&page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Student detail
GET {{host}}/api/admin/students/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ---- Admin: Administrators (needs an Admin / SuperAdmin token) ----

### List staff (filters: search, role, status, page, pageSize)
GET {{host}}/api/admin/administrators?role=Reviewer&status=Active
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Assignable roles
GET {{host}}/api/admin/administrators/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Add administrator (sends an invitation email)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/administrators
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Jane Doe", "email": "jane.doe@example.com", "role": "Reviewer", "status": "Active" }

### Edit administrator (same body; use status "Inactive" to deactivate)
PUT {{host}}/api/admin/administrators/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Jane Doe", "email": "jane.doe@example.com", "role": "Content manager", "status": "Active" }

### Resend invitation (only for accounts that have never signed in)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/administrators/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/resend-invitation
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
